Jonadab the Unsightly One wrote:
(snip)

Just replying to this thread generally, I thought I'd give a status
report. I'd like to give huge thanks to Jonadab the Unsightly One for
testing these bugs in NetHack 4, to Grunt for fixing many of them, and
to Sean Hunt for porting the fixes from GruntHack to NetHack 4.

So far out of the bugs that Jonadab has investigated, we have:
- 8 bugs that definitely exist in NH4 and have not yet been fixed;
- 3 bugs where it is debatable whether they are actually bugs;
- 16 bugs which have been fixed in other variants (mostly GruntHack);
- 39 bugs that were explicitly fixed in NH4;
- 6 bugs that were fixed as a side effect of other changes in NH4;
- 6 bugs where further information exists on the wiki;
- 4 bugs that are inapplicable to NH4;
- and 18 bugs we haven't managed to pin down yet.

For someone who merely plays NetHack, rather than codes it, those 19 are
the most important to find; you can look for them either in NetHack 4,
or in vanilla, or even in some other variant. Here they are:

C341-5 When you see your pet move, the pet may be referred to as "it".
C342-13 Hangup can cause loss of objects being moved internally. 
C342-31 You can get a message telling you a monster wields a weapon it
already was wielding.
C343-1  At a pit the game can give messages with poor grammar. 
C343-12 There are a number of places that misuse "your".
C343-23 Dungeon collapses after vault guard fails to lead you out. 
C343-27 Kicked objects do not slide properly on air or water levels.
C343-33 Sometimes a monster may remain hidden under a corpse that has
rotted away.
C343-46 Breaking up a boulder or statue can result in pieces that are
described incorrectly.
C343-48 Killing your pet doesn't get you any experience when it should.
C343-53 If a shopkeeper is trapped adjacent to the door, the game may
get confused and issue impossible or panic messages. (We've made some
progress in working this one out here on rgrn over the past few days,
though.)
C343-60 Several messages delivered when hero's fingers are slippery have
poor grammar.
C343-62 Riding into a magic portal gives an extra, useless message.
C343-66 Co-aligned unicorns in a bones file may be hostile. 
C343-68 Incorrect message may be given when a spellcasting monster
summons other monsters.
C343-75 Eating Medusa's corpse may not work properly (theory I just had
writing this post: can it be eaten the same way as Rider corpses?)
C343-78 Digging in an existing hole charges you for the time it takes to
dig the whole hole.
C343-79 "Mr." or "Ms." may show up in front of names when it should not.

